    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the crash successfully. The ASAN output confirms the exact vulnerability path: a SEGV write in `str_init_embed` at `string.c:73`, called through `str_new` → `mrb_str_new` → `unpack_hex` → `pack_unpack` → `mrb_pack_unpack`.\n\nThe PoC `\"A\".unpack(\"H2147483648\")` triggers an integer overflow: the template count 2147483648 (2^31) is parsed as a 64-bit `mrb_int` but truncated to 32-bit `int`, wrapping to -2147483648. This negative value bypasses the `-1` wildcard check in `unpack_hex`, gets passed to `mrb_str_new` as a negative length, and causes an out-of-bounds write in `str_init_embed` when it indexes the embedded string buffer at a negative offset.",
